E1. dim of connected drift conserving a record (0 = no such drift)
    system            record         real QM   complex QM   classical  boxworld
    2      (N=2)   complete(2)       0          1          0         0
    3      (N=3)   complete(3)       0          2          0         -
    3      (N=3)   two states         0          2          0         -
    4      (N=4)   complete(4)       0          3          0         -
    4      (N=4)   two states         1          5          0         -
    2x2    (N=4)   complete(4)       0          3          0         0
    2x2    (N=4)   two states         1          5          0         0
    2x3    (N=6)   complete(6)       0          5          0         0
    2x3    (N=6)   two states         6         17          0         0
    3x3    (N=9)   complete(9)       0          8          0         0
    3x3    (N=9)   two states        21         50          0         0
    analytic: real QM complete record -> generators antisymmetric AND diagonal -> 0 for every N.
              complex QM complete record -> diagonal phases U(1)^N / U(1) -> N-1 >= 1 for every N>=2.
              quaternionic QM complete record -> Sp(1)^N -> 3N (passes; known to lack good composites).

E2. multi-frequency orbits t -> (cos t, sin t, r cos kt, r sin kt) (a circle group acting with weights 1 and k on R^4)
    weights (1,2), r=0.5: quarter-phase identity p0+p2=p1+p3 holds? False;  best linear copier residual = 2.000e-01
    weights (1,3), r=0.5: quarter-phase identity p0+p2=p1+p3 holds? True;  best linear copier residual = 4.000e-01
    weights (1,2), r=1.0: quarter-phase identity p0+p2=p1+p3 holds? False;  best linear copier residual = 2.500e-01
    -> round-1 four-point step does not apply to these orbits, but no copier exists; the frequency-doubling proof (NOTE R2a') covers them.

E3. discrete ticks
    random reversible map on 12 states: orbit period = 9; a tracker that has stored one period predicts with error 0 forever.
    irrational rotation, tracker with 1 bits of phase, later question at a random tick up to 1e6: error = 0.256 (~1/(2*2^m)=0.250); never decays without new acquisition
    irrational rotation, tracker with 2 bits of phase, later question at a random tick up to 1e6: error = 0.125 (~1/(2*2^m)=0.125); never decays without new acquisition
    irrational rotation, tracker with 4 bits of phase, later question at a random tick up to 1e6: error = 0.038 (~1/(2*2^m)=0.031); never decays without new acquisition
    irrational rotation, tracker with 6 bits of phase, later question at a random tick up to 1e6: error = 0.005 (~1/(2*2^m)=0.008); never decays without new acquisition
